MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of All Things to Come and Master of Puppets appeal to me because they combine heaviness with intricate rhythms or extended arrangements, connecting with my recent interest in Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days.",
    "Through the Eyes and Something Like Human also feel natural because I still enjoy heavy music with strong melodies, as reflected in my listening to One Day Remains."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Load and Three Days Grace fit parts of my taste, but they are less compelling today because I am prioritizing rhythmic complexity and intensity over a more straightforward hard rock sound.",
    "I passed on Panic and Lines In My Face because I could not confidently connect those titles to music I wanted to hear; that uncertainty does not mean I dislike their sound."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat a broad connection to heavy rock as enough, even though some heavy albums fit my current mood much more closely than others.",
    "Recommending several Metallica albums captures my interest in metal, but those albums are not interchangeable for me: I would choose Master of Puppets ahead of Kill Em All for its more developed arrangements."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listening to Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days makes heavy grooves, intricate rhythms, and longer musical development especially appealing right now.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose this session; I passed on Dirt and Three Days Grace because other choices felt more compelling today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in melodic heavy music, but only some capture my current preference for intensity paired with rhythmic and structural complexity."
}
